WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:55.980
<b>Pirates vs. CP9</b>

3
00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.080
This is probably the place.

4
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.440
I finally made it.

5
00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.430
I had to go
up and down all those stairs.

6
00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:09.410
Robin!

7
00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.900
Hey! Robin!

8
00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.590
It's me!

9
00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.090
Robin!

10
00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:20.000
Where are you?!

11
00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.370
Dammit!

12
00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:27.080
That damn pigeon guy!

13
00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.800
Oh, yeah...!

14
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.630
I know where they're going.

15
00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.160
I should just head to the
Gates of Justice, too!

16
00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.050
You have the key
to Robin's handcuffs, right?

17
00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.390
Want to give it to me
before I take you down?

18
00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.810
That's a foolish question.

19
00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:49.370
I was disappointed that I didn't
get to see your real ability...

20
00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:51.540
at the Galley-La mansion.

21
00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:55.730
I never thought that pirates
would come this far, either, so...

22
00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.450
Be careful;
I've grown far stronger since then.

23
00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:04.750
I can imagine,
with all that energy you've got...

24
00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.910
Energy like that of a beast.

25
00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.720
What a fearsome man you are.

26
00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:11.920
However,

27
00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:16.790
my swordsmanship is the best in CP9.

28
00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.460
Don't underestimate me.

29
00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:20.800
Two-Sword Style, huh?

30
00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:27.500
Tempest Kick.

31
00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:40.240
So, no... sorry, but I use four swords.

32
00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.860
No problem.

33
00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:44.410
Come to think of it,
your entire body is a weapon.

34
00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.210
72...

35
00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:01.880
Tempest Kick.

36
00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.340
– Pound Phoenix!
– White Thunder!

37
00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:09.160
Shave!

38
00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.070
This is fun!

39
00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:33.620
I don't have time to have fun!

40
00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.730
Then you just have to take me down.

41
00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:40.340
Tempest Kick!

42
00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:41.240
Tumult!

43
00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.840
He controls these slashing attacks so easily.

44
00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.110
You bastard... Are you mocking me?

45
00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:06.070
Whoa... I'd expect no less from you.

46
00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:08.870
If you're in that much
of a hurry, I'll show you...

47
00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:12.750
my new powers.

48
00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.310
Wh... What the hell?!

49
00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.530
At any rate, what the heck is this room?

50
00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:51.250
Someone really went nuts on the gardening.

51
00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.120
This is practically outside!

52
00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:54.640
No, no...

53
00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:57.210
More importantly, I have to get
the key to Robin's handcuffs right now!

54
00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.490
That key...!

55
00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:05.090
Quietly...

56
00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.790
Don't hesitate!

57
00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:12.770
If I quietly grab it,

58
00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:15.560
then quietly run away...

59
00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.950
I'll accomplish my mission.

60
00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:20.020
It'll be a flawless victory!

61
00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.290
That's right.

62
00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:25.110
I'm the king of being lucky!

63
00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.250
I'm almost there!

64
00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.210
A-A rooster?!

65
00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:48.880
Oh, no! What is the noisiest
bird of them all doing here?

66
00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:51.920
Oh, no!

67
00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:53.310
If it crows, it's all over!

68
00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:56.140
If it crows, he'll get up,
find me, and kill me!

69
00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:57.070
Hey.

70
00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:58.400
What're you looking at?!

71
00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.540
Are you trying to crow?

72
00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:01.270
Are you?! Are you?!

73
00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:03.610
Shhh! Shhh!

74
00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:06.220
Rooster-kun! Rooster-san!
Rooster-sama! I beg you!

75
00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:07.840
Please don't crow!

76
00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:11.250
Don't crow!
Don't! Please don't!

77
00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:14.450
No rooster would crow like that!

78
00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:17.660
Oh, you're here, pirate.

79
00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.620
Th-That damn rooster!

80
00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:23.080
Well, I guess it's time
I give you a beatdown.

81
00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.920
That damn rooster!

82
00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.180
H-He's strong...

83
00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.100
So you're the one who came?!

84
00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:47.540
You're the one who shot through
the government flag, right?

85
00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:50.660
Jug reads "Liquor".

86
00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:54.020
It seems that you're a skilled sniper.

87
00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:01.160
He delivered a punch like that
right after he woke up?

88
00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:04.020
Sorry for attacking you half-assed.

89
00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:05.000
Forgive me.

90
00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:08.420
It must've hurt.

91
00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:17.890
Huh?

92
00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.930
Don't worry.

93
00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:23.310
I may not look like it,
but I'm not into tormenting my opponent.

94
00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:27.020
A-A devil fruit...!

95
00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:29.980
The Dog Dog Fruit, Model: Wolf!

96
00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:33.250
I'll just tear out your windpipe
and that'll be it.

97
00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:34.730
You'll die anyway.

98
00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:37.310
You don't have to suffer.

99
00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:38.950
Isn't that right?

100
00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:40.710
W-Wolf...!

101
00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:44.670
D-Dammit!

102
00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:47.520
What?! Are you gonna fight?

103
00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:49.420
You don't look strong, though.

104
00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:53.390
S-Strong or not, I'm gonna fight!

105
00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.250
Shut up!

106
00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:58.600
I came to rescue Robin!

107
00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:02.270
Whoa! The ceiling is...

108
00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:04.560
collapsing!

109
00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:07.960
Oh, shoot!

110
00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:09.570
I was gonna
stop the transformation...

111
00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:11.610
when I reached my hybrid form,
but I became a giraffe!

112
00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:15.070
A talking giraffe is falling toward us!

113
00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:17.630
Kaku!

114
00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:20.580
That power of yours is too cool!

115
00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:21.840
A wolf?!

116
00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:24.410
What is this place?! A zoo?!

117
00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:36.220
The Ox Ox Fruit, Model: Giraffe!

118
00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:39.660
You poor guy!

119
00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:41.970
To think that you'll be
a giraffe man for the rest of your life!

120
00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:46.070
What's wrong with giraffes?!

121
00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:48.900
I said I like it!

122
00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:53.000
That pigeon guy
was a leopard, wasn't he?

123
00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:56.360
There are two more ability users who transform into animals...

124
00:09:56.710 --> 00:10:00.070
Is CP9 that kind of group?

125
00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:05.770
S-So they are zoan-type ability users?

126
00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:07.700
A wolf man and a giraffe man...

127
00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.340
I got stuck with a scary one!

128
00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:14.160
But Zoro falling with that giraffe saved me.

129
00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:16.210
While it appears to be a two-versus-two fight,

130
00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.510
I'll just wait for Zoro to do most of the work.

131
00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.360
What's that?

132
00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:23.850
It looks like a safe
with the door left opened.

133
00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:24.770
Whoa!

134
00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:27.310
Could those
weird-looking handcuffs be...?!

135
00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:30.900
I said don't laugh!

136
00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.080
Hey, giraffe!

137
00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:35.740
Just how long are you gonna
stand there arguing with him?

138
00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:38.700
I thought I told you
that I don't have much time.

139
00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:43.330
If you wanna keep arguing,
I'll just cut you down where you stand.

140
00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:48.250
How foolish... Don't underestimate a
giraffe's limitless destructive power.

141
00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.080
Transform...

142
00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:52.670
Hybrid Form!

143
00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:55.810
I'll show you...

144
00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:59.530
the power of my transformation!

145
00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:13.000
How lame!

146
00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:13.990
Gasp!

147
00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:15.900
What'd you just...?

148
00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:23.210
Why'd I blurt something like that out?!

149
00:11:23.210 --> 00:11:24.040
I shouldn't have said that.

150
00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:26.870
I was so shocked
that I just blurted it out!

151
00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:29.200
Don't lose your composure, Zoro!
It will dull your blades!

152
00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:34.840
Just how long are you gonna
keep laughing, Jabra?!

153
00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:36.820
S-Sorry.

154
00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.920
In any case, he looks funny.

155
00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:42.680
How the hell does this form
reflect his square features?

156
00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:48.160
Wh-What're these handcuffs?!

157
00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:49.730
Ahhh!

158
00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:52.080
Shoot! I'm sorry, Zoro-kun!

159
00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.060
Hey! What're you doing?!

160
00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:59.220
Th-They're probably seastone handcuffs just like Robin's!

161
00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:01.950
Since our enemies are both
devil fruit ability users.

162
00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:04.820
I thought they'd be weaker if
they were handcuffed with them!

163
00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:08.120
So why are they on me, you idiot?!

164
00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:09.980
B-Because...

165
00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:15.500
the giraffe's face is so
funny that I just lost my grip.

166
00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:19.080
A giraffe with square everything...

167
00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:22.310
He's right!

168
00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:26.510
Damn all of you!

169
00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:32.100
Taste the power of an ability user!

170
00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:34.970
Tempest Kick!

171
00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:40.720
Whoa! What's that?!

172
00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:42.190
He's gonna do something!

173
00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:45.280
Sky Slicer!

174
00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:50.280
This isn't good.

175
00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:52.200
Duck, Usopp!

176
00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:16.440
I see...

177
00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:19.310
Your strength is in your length—
in other words, your reach.

178
00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:23.110
With the power coming from that huge
body and the centrifugal force,

179
00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:26.080
your attacks are deeper
and sharper than before.

180
00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.840
Wh-What the heck?!

181
00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:33.870
Hey, I don't see any damage.

182
00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:35.210
Look at the ceiling.

183
00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:38.080
Huh? The ceiling?

184
00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:39.750
Oh?

185
00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:41.740
I can see the blue sky.

186
00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:44.890
Whoa...

187
00:13:44.890 --> 00:13:46.220
I wonder why... Hm...?

188
00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:51.470
Don't tell me the
Tower of Justice has been cut in two!

189
00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:53.720
Hey, hey, hey, hey...!

190
00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:54.960
This is dangerous!

191
00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:57.850
How shameful!

192
00:13:57.860 --> 00:14:00.640
You betrayed your emotions during a battle!

193
00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:02.130
Shut up.

194
00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:04.480
I like being a giraffe.

195
00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:06.650
I love giraffes.

196
00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:09.280
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

197
00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:13.110
No matter how sharp your attacks are,

198
00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:16.450
they won't intimidate me at all.

199
00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.280
S-Stop it, Zoro!

200
00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:21.880
That hurts! What're you doing?!

201
00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.150
Why are you pulling my arm?!

202
00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:27.240
Huh...? Pulling my arm?

203
00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:36.270
Whoa! It's locked tight!

204
00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:38.550
Hey! What're you doing?!

205
00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:40.480
It's not my fault, is it?!

206
00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:43.440
This happened because you charged at me!

207
00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:46.680
I did that because you were standing
there in a daze when he attacked!

208
00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:48.450
Just unlock these handcuffs!

209
00:14:52.930 --> 00:14:55.370
What're these guys doing?

210
00:14:56.030 --> 00:14:57.310
Beats me.

211
00:14:58.360 --> 00:14:59.970
To put it simply,

212
00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:03.370
this means that we're
in the same situation as Robin is.

213
00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:04.630
Then, the key is...

214
00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.960
in the hands of one
of the CP9 members.

215
00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:08.630
We have no choice but to beat them and get their keys.

216
00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:11.960
Don't be absurd!
There's no way we can fight like this!

217
00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:14.340
Our prey are locked together.

218
00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:16.030
Okay then, Jabra.

219
00:15:16.030 --> 00:15:19.640
Just stand back
and leave these two to me.

220
00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:24.150
What?! Are you trying to snatch my prey?!

221
00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:27.860
So, do you want to work
together and fight them?

222
00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:30.310
I'd rather die.

223
00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:31.450
Me, too.

224
00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:32.650
Hey, you two!

225
00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:35.120
Tell us the number on those handcuffs.

226
00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:36.950
Number?

227
00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:40.880
The handcuffs and the keys have numbers

228
00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:44.200
so that we know which key
unlocks which handcuffs.

229
00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:46.870
If those handcuffs can be unlocked
by one of the keys we have,

230
00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:48.440
we'll unlock them right away.

231
00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:50.130
What?! Really?!

232
00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:51.630
The number... where's the number?

233
00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:53.850
Here it is! It's 2!

234
00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:55.100
Unlock them!

235
00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:57.760
Not the right one.

236
00:15:57.780 --> 00:15:59.470
Mine isn't, either.

237
00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:00.310
Sorry.

238
00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:03.210
What?! You got my hopes up, you jerks!

239
00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:04.510
Damn it!

240
00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:07.980
Then, it means one of the other three
CP9 members has the right one, huh?

241
00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:10.150
I guess we have no choice.

242
00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:12.910
The first one to get a kill wins.

243
00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:14.470
Seems like that's the only way.

244
00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:16.660
What?!

245
00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:21.800
What?!

246
00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:27.670
<b>Tower of Justice
Inner Chamber</b>

247
00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:30.670
Whoa! What's with these stairs?!

248
00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:33.170
They're sliced in two and out of place.

249
00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:38.780
The impact from earlier...

250
00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:41.480
As I suspected,
something must've happened.

251
00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:43.730
Is this building okay?

252
00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:54.790
Hey! Are you okay?!

253
00:17:02.570 --> 00:17:05.370
Ah! Zoro! Sogeking!

254
00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:09.380
Ah! Hey! Chopper!

255
00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:13.450
What's going on? They're waving to me.

256
00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:15.070
It looks kinda fun.

257
00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:18.300
H-Hey, guys!

258
00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:22.180
Idiot!

259
00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:23.880
Look at the handcuffs!

260
00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:26.850
Find the key for the no. 2 handcuffs!

261
00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.310
Huh? A key?

262
00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:37.410
What the hell is this?!

263
00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:41.100
I just assumed that there'd
be a bridge or something.

264
00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:45.290
What crazy huge whirlpools!

265
00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:48.090
I can see the Gates of Justice now,

266
00:17:48.090 --> 00:17:50.170
but is it possible to get
there on a regular boat?

267
00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:52.770
Whatever. I don't have much time.

268
00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:54.300
I guess I'll try something.

269
00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.050
Here we go!

270
00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:59.470
Just wait, Robin!

271
00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:03.850
I see.

272
00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:07.060
So the handcuffs and the keys
have numbers on them.

273
00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:08.720
What?!

274
00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:10.550
That's what's happening here?

275
00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:12.270
Then I'll fight these guys!

276
00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:13.760
Don't be ridiculous!

277
00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:16.530
There are two of them!
 If you get taken out,

278
00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:19.610
with these handcuffs on, we're dead for sure!

279
00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:22.660
Please! You're our only hope!

280
00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:24.060
Hope?

281
00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:26.700
It's not like I'm
happy to hear that, you jerk!

282
00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.100
Sanji, Nami, and Franky...

283
00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:33.210
If any of them get the no. 2 key, bring it straight to us!

284
00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:34.940
We're counting on you!

285
00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:38.630
The one who's likely to get
the key first is... maybe Sanji?

286
00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:43.180
I'll go look for Sanji.

287
00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:45.100
I'm their only hope!

288
00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:57.490
Now...

289
00:18:57.490 --> 00:19:03.200
<b>Level 0 
Isolated Corridor
Nami vs. Kumadori</b>

290
00:18:57.490 --> 00:19:02.260
I've got you!

291
00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:04.830
Let me go!

292
00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:09.210
Yoyoi!

293
00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:11.840
Just...

294
00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:15.210
give up!

295
00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:18.380
Die!

296
00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:29.330
I'm no match for him at all!

297
00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:35.320
Franky...

298
00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:37.780
Iron Body!

299
00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:39.090
Boxing!

300
00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:45.950
Shave!

301
00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:53.330
<b>Hallway in Front of the Pantry
Franky vs. Fukuro</b>

302
00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:51.420
What's with your punches?

303
00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:53.330
You're no ordinary human!

304
00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:57.330
Even if you harden your body to make it like iron,

305
00:19:57.330 --> 00:20:00.470
my fists are real iron.

306
00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:05.510
N-No!

307
00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:08.390
This is no time for having tea!

308
00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:14.900
<b>Kalifa's Room
Sanji vs. Kalifa</b>

309
00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.100
Witchcraft!

310
00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:13.260
I was drawn in by your witchcraft!

311
00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:17.860
I almost fell victim to a love trap as dangerous as a storm surge!

312
00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:21.400
You've already had three cups.

313
00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:23.780
Shut up, witch!

314
00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.620
I'm not gonna
be caught in a trap again!

315
00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:29.870
CP9 insulted Robin-chan
terribly on the sea train.

316
00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:31.330
I'm not gonna forget about it.

317
00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:38.290
Now...

318
00:20:38.850 --> 00:20:40.710
give me the key!

319
00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:43.120
That's too bad...

320
00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:45.740
It seems like you're in a hurry.

321
00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:49.790
Go ahead and take the key.

322
00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:52.980
Where is it?

323
00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:54.940
Well...

324
00:20:55.300 --> 00:20:59.570
Where on my body do you think I hid it?

325
00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:02.280
Why don't you try finding it?

326
00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:06.450
I'd be happy to!

327
00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:13.160
It's looking hopeless for you.

328
00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:16.080
I'm an idiot.
